     "caption": "A cumulative frequency graph for 80 marks with the median read at 33.3.",
     "alt": "A rising curve from 0 to 80 with dashed lines showing the median at cumulative frequency 40."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Reading the curve",
     "md": "To find how many pupils scored more than 40: read the cumulative frequency at 40 (56) and subtract from the total: 80 − 56 = 24. By interpolating inside the class we may calculate: median position 40, so median = 30 + (40 − 32) ÷ 24 × 10 = 33.3. Q₁ at position 20: 20 + (20 − 14) ÷ 18 × 10 = 23.3. Q₃ at position 60: 42.9."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Plotting at the middle of the class instead of the upper boundary.\n- Forgetting to start the curve at zero.\n- Using the frequency (not the cumulative frequency) to find the median position."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1: median and quartiles",
     "statement": "From the cumulative frequencies 4, 14, 32, 56, 70, 78, 80 for classes of width 10 from 0 to 70, estimate the median, the quartiles and the interquartile range.",
     "steps": [
      "Median at position 40 lies in the class 30–40: 30 + (40 − 32) ÷ 24 × 10 = 33.3.",
      "Q₁ at position 20 is in 20–30: 20 + (20 − 14) ÷ 18 × 10 = 23.3. Q₃ at 60 is in 40–50: 40 + (60 − 56) ÷ 14 × 10 = 42.9.",
      "IQR = 42.9 − 23.3 = 19.5."
     ],
     "answer": "**Median ≈ 33.3; Q₁ ≈ 23.3; Q₃ ≈ 42.9; IQR ≈ 19.5.**",
